<h2>What you're hearing</h2>
<p>A real minute of a Hebrew podcast, with no editing on our side. The second version went through the same code that runs in the app, with the same settings, and nothing else about it changed.</p>
<p>The best way to hear it: press play, wait for the guest to start talking, and switch between the versions without stopping. The player carries on from the exact same second.</p>

<h2>What the numbers mean</h2>
<p><strong>The gap between speakers</strong> is the difference between the quiet and the loud parts of this minute. In the original it is <span dir="ltr">7.1 dB</span>. After levelling it is <span dir="ltr">2.9 dB</span>. That gap is what sends your hand to the knob.</p>
<p><strong>The overall level</strong> went up, from <span dir="ltr">-20.7 dBFS</span> to <span dir="ltr">-18.1 dBFS</span>. That number matters because there is a cheap way to close a gap: turn everything down. The opposite happened here. The quiet voice came up, so the episode as a whole sounds louder, not softer.</p>

